 ### Flat Rank
-A space-efficient approach for answering rank queries on bit vectors in constant time [S2]. It partitions the bit vector into blocks and stores the cumulative count of 1-bits up to each block in an auxiliary array [S2]. This method requires approximately 3.51% additional space overhead compared to the raw bit vector [S2]. It is chosen when the bit vector is large and frequent rank queries are needed, trading memory for query speed, whereas Prefix Rank is typically used for small, fixed-size nodes (e.g., 8 bits) where no auxiliary storage is needed [S2].
